Task 9.4: Implement theme system

Summary:
Created a comprehensive theme system with dark/light mode switching and color impaired mode support.

Changes Made:
1. Created /app/src/lib/theme/ThemeProvider.tsx
   - Theme context with 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto' options
   - Persist theme preference to localStorage
   - Sync with system preference when 'auto' is selected
   - Apply CSS classes to document root based on theme
   - Manages color impaired mode state

2. Created /app/src/lib/theme/useTheme.ts
   - Returns current theme, setTheme function, and toggle function
   - Handles system preference detection
   - Throws error when used outside ThemeProvider

3. Created /app/src/lib/theme/colorImpaired.ts
   - Utility to toggle color impaired mode
   - Applies CSS classes for color blind accessibility
   - Persists preference to localStorage

4. Updated /app/src/components/providers/AppProviders.tsx
   - Wrapped app with ThemeProvider

5. Created theme module index.ts for clean exports

6. CSS variables already existed in globals.css:
   - Dark mode theme tokens defined
   - Light mode theme tokens with [data-theme='light'] selector
   - Color impaired mode tokens with [data-color-impaired='true'] selector

7. Created comprehensive tests:
   - ThemeProvider.test.tsx (6 tests)
   - useTheme.test.tsx (3 tests)
   - colorImpaired.test.ts (11 tests)
   - All tests passing with >80% coverage

Note: The UI settings page at /app/src/app/(shell)/settings/ui/page.tsx already had theme selector and color impaired mode toggle, which now integrates with the new theme system through the ThemeProvider context.

Why:
To provide a React context-based theme system that:
- Is easier to use in components than imperative API
- Maintains consistent state across the app
- Provides type-safe theme management
- Follows React best practices with hooks
- Improves accessibility with color impaired mode
- Maintains user preferences across sessions
